WEBVTT

00:08.216 --> 00:09.384
Let's move!

00:21.688 --> 00:22.522
Hanji?

00:23.481 --> 00:25.066
Get me a horse.

00:25.984 --> 00:28.445
Section Commander!
Where are you trying to go?

00:29.237 --> 00:32.574
To that village where we captured
the Titan who couldn't walk.

00:33.074 --> 00:34.367
Do you mean Ragako?

00:34.659 --> 00:36.703
I need to see it with my own eyes.

00:36.953 --> 00:38.872
Don't say something so ridiculous!

00:39.247 --> 00:42.000
Your body can't ride a horse right now!

00:44.377 --> 00:47.839
I have a feeling
that we need to investigate...

00:51.342 --> 00:52.218
All right.

00:54.179 --> 00:57.766
I'll go there on my own,
so you stay here and faint or something.

01:04.397 --> 01:07.025
Spread out!
Take formation to locate any enemies!

01:17.869 --> 01:18.703
Eren...

02:57.760 --> 02:58.636
Oh, Eren.

03:00.054 --> 03:00.972
You're awake?

03:21.034 --> 03:21.993
What the hell?

03:22.702 --> 03:23.578
My arms!

03:24.954 --> 03:25.788
Eren.

03:26.497 --> 03:28.958
Look at me. I'm in the same shape as you.

03:30.001 --> 03:32.003
I guess both of us are having a bad day.

03:32.795 --> 03:33.630
Ymir...

03:34.714 --> 03:37.175
why don't I have any arms?

03:37.759 --> 03:38.760
That's my bad.

03:39.302 --> 03:40.595
I did that.

03:43.056 --> 03:44.807
I was kind of in a hurry.

03:45.600 --> 03:47.477
When I rushed to bite your nape,

03:47.852 --> 03:50.313
I neglected to take your arms
into account.

03:53.733 --> 03:54.609
I see...

03:55.818 --> 03:58.279
I must have lost...

04:08.998 --> 04:10.208
Stop, Eren!

04:10.833 --> 04:12.293
Hold on for a while.

04:13.211 --> 04:14.796
Take a good look around us.

04:15.672 --> 04:18.633
We're in a giant forest within Wall Maria.

04:19.300 --> 04:21.886
It's not even close to any of the walls.

04:22.845 --> 04:26.099
In other words,
we're deep in Titan territory.

04:26.808 --> 04:27.642
Look.

04:28.601 --> 04:31.062
I think that one down there
is an Abnormal.

04:32.063 --> 04:37.026
It looks like he's just relaxing,
but he's not taking his eyes off us.

04:38.027 --> 04:39.904
There are a lot of small ones
down there too.

04:40.154 --> 04:41.698
That alone is dangerous.

04:42.490 --> 04:44.117
Another big one is over there.

04:45.493 --> 04:47.453
He's staring at us,
but won't come any closer.

04:48.371 --> 04:50.456
I bet you that one's a scaredy-cat.

04:52.041 --> 04:53.876
And then you've got these chumps.

04:54.460 --> 04:55.837
Those dirty bastards.

04:56.337 --> 04:58.965
They're the only ones
with any ODM gear on.

04:59.882 --> 05:01.884
Reiner's wearing your gear.

05:02.760 --> 05:06.723
At this point, changing into a Titan
is not going to solve anything.

05:07.223 --> 05:09.392
Not only can they do that,

05:09.642 --> 05:12.103
but they can escape high
into the trees as well.

05:12.478 --> 05:15.315
Those two aside,
there are Titans all around us.

05:16.024 --> 05:20.987
Escaping from this Titan territory
would be tough, even with Titan powers.

05:22.697 --> 05:23.656
Understand?

05:24.282 --> 05:26.326
There's nothing to gain
by acting like that.

05:27.493 --> 05:28.328
No.

05:29.203 --> 05:31.622
You two can't even turn into Titans now,

05:32.040 --> 05:34.459
so don't count on that to help you.

05:35.543 --> 05:37.045
Your body has reached its limits.

05:37.503 --> 05:40.882
It's taking everything you've got
to repair the damage.

05:43.009 --> 05:43.926
Are you stupid?

05:44.302 --> 05:47.013
Why the hell would I trust your words?

05:51.559 --> 05:52.393
Well...

05:52.685 --> 05:56.981
it's not like I know
how Titan powers work.

05:57.815 --> 06:01.235
Unlike you guys,
I'm pretty clueless about it.

06:02.236 --> 06:03.654
Hey, Reiner.

06:04.489 --> 06:07.200
You said you would talk once Eren woke up.

06:08.034 --> 06:11.245
It's about time one of you said
what you are planning to do with us.

06:14.248 --> 06:16.250
We'll take you to our hometown.

06:17.585 --> 06:20.963
I realize that you're not going to listen
and do as I say.

06:21.839 --> 06:25.760
But like Ymir was saying,
this place is swarming with Titans.

06:26.177 --> 06:28.096
We could beat the hell out
of each other right now,

06:28.846 --> 06:31.766
but when we're weak, the other Titans
would just come and eat us.

06:32.934 --> 06:35.061
So until nightfall,
when the Titans can't move,

06:35.728 --> 06:37.855
we have no choice but to wait here.

06:38.856 --> 06:41.067
Whether you're trying to run from us

06:41.692 --> 06:44.112
or you're going to let us take you away,

06:45.029 --> 06:46.531
either way, we wait for the night.

06:48.157 --> 06:51.160
Why didn't you stay as the Armored Titan
and run home?

06:51.828 --> 06:54.205
What's the point of stopping here?

06:54.747 --> 06:56.624
Too tired and needed a break?

06:57.792 --> 06:59.961
Why don't you use your imagination?

07:04.173 --> 07:05.007
Think...

07:06.134 --> 07:08.177
If I waited for an opening
and became a Titan,

07:08.803 --> 07:12.807
running away from here
wouldn't seem to be a challenge.

07:14.058 --> 07:17.770
But can I transform
into a Titan in the first place?

07:19.939 --> 07:21.816
Reiner said that I can't.

07:22.233 --> 07:26.362
I have to consider that even Reiner
had to stop here to take a break.

07:27.363 --> 07:29.866
If my Titan form isn't strong enough,

07:30.199 --> 07:32.660
does that mean I'll just get eaten
by the others?

07:35.872 --> 07:38.875
Are you simply waiting here for nightfall?

07:39.083 --> 07:40.460
Maybe I am.

07:40.960 --> 07:44.297
No. There's no way they would wait
until nightfall.

07:44.755 --> 07:48.301
They're not going to give our bodies
the chance to fully recover.

07:49.510 --> 07:52.305
They'll make their move
while we're still powerless.

07:54.724 --> 07:56.767
I can't do anything at the moment.

07:57.185 --> 07:58.269
At this rate...

08:01.856 --> 08:03.399
What happened to everybody?

08:04.233 --> 08:05.443
Where are the Scouts?

08:09.864 --> 08:12.200
Don't tell me they're coming this way.

08:12.450 --> 08:15.286
If they try to help,
no one's going to make it back safely.

08:15.369 --> 08:19.499
Why? The Titans at the castle
moved just fine at night.

08:20.208 --> 08:21.709
Won't these Titans too?

08:22.376 --> 08:24.670
The Titans here can't move at night.

08:25.213 --> 08:28.382
You should know all about it, Ymir.

08:31.761 --> 08:34.639
Speaking of which,
why can Ymir turn into a Titan?

08:35.389 --> 08:38.351
I don't think she's like me,
who knew nothing about it.

08:39.310 --> 08:40.394
Is she on our side?

08:41.187 --> 08:43.314
I don't even know what her goal is.

08:43.981 --> 08:46.484
It's hard enough to understand her.

08:49.237 --> 08:50.321
I've made up my mind.

08:51.280 --> 08:54.242
Right now, what I need is information.

08:55.284 --> 08:58.120
I need to find out
everything I can from them.

08:58.871 --> 09:00.957
And then I'll make my escape.

09:02.375 --> 09:04.168
To do that, I need to...

09:06.420 --> 09:08.130
overcome all my emotions...

09:09.465 --> 09:11.467
and wait for my body to heal.

09:15.846 --> 09:18.307
Titan spotted at three o'clock!
Fire the signal!

09:19.767 --> 09:22.019
Smoke shell confirmed on the right-wing!

09:22.520 --> 09:23.646
Do not change direction!

09:23.896 --> 09:27.024
Have the right-wing merge in the center
and stay on course!

09:27.441 --> 09:29.110
We only have until sunset!

09:29.527 --> 09:31.904
We must take the shortest possible path!

09:35.157 --> 09:36.075
Mikasa.

09:36.909 --> 09:37.994
Hey, Mikasa!

09:38.578 --> 09:39.537
Mikasa!

09:40.746 --> 09:42.206
Stop pushing so hard.

09:42.665 --> 09:46.752
You're drifting near the vanguard.
It will ruin the whole formation.

09:47.753 --> 09:50.631
I know how you feel,
but didn't I tell you?

09:50.881 --> 09:54.010
Eren won't get taken away
without putting up a fight.

09:54.802 --> 09:55.720
Don't you agree?

09:58.264 --> 10:00.349
You know he'll never give up.

10:00.600 --> 10:04.478
So it's up to us to stay calm
and be there when he needs us.

10:08.858 --> 10:10.401
Just like we did back then.

10:34.175 --> 10:35.009
Reiner,

10:35.635 --> 10:36.802
you got any water?

10:37.511 --> 10:40.389
If I don't get some soon,
I'm going to shrivel up and die.

10:41.015 --> 10:45.811
Even if it's a matter of life and death,
there's nothing we can do now.

10:47.229 --> 10:51.525
He's completely right.
This situation couldn't be any worse.

10:54.403 --> 10:55.821
Speaking of which...

10:56.155 --> 10:58.282
Ever since the Titans showed up
yesterday morning,

10:58.532 --> 11:01.285
we've been working our asses off.

11:02.078 --> 11:05.247
With nothing to eat or drink
and no sleep at all.

11:06.123 --> 11:09.585
Fortunately,
the wall wasn't broken or anything.

11:10.252 --> 11:12.421
I think we deserve a break.

11:13.339 --> 11:15.508
We'll see about getting promoted later.

11:17.051 --> 11:17.885
Reiner...

11:19.762 --> 11:23.474
What? We've done plenty to deserve it.

11:24.517 --> 11:28.354
We've performed outstandingly,
considering everything we've been through.

11:29.438 --> 11:32.817
I know soldiers like us are expected
to fulfill their duties...

11:33.651 --> 11:35.444
but I think we've earned it.

11:42.410 --> 11:43.661
Reiner...

11:44.662 --> 11:46.789
What are you talking about?

11:47.248 --> 11:49.083
What? What do you mean?

11:49.375 --> 11:52.711
I'm not saying we're demanding
to be promoted to captains.

11:53.045 --> 11:55.256
That's not what I mean.

11:55.631 --> 11:59.510
Oh, yes.
Where did you get that cannon from?

12:00.010 --> 12:02.096
That really saved my life.

12:04.223 --> 12:06.725
It's a good thing Christa helped me
after that.

12:07.309 --> 12:09.979
To be honest,
I think she has a thing for me.

12:10.229 --> 12:11.063
Hey...

12:11.272 --> 12:14.316
Now that I think about it,
Christa has always treated me especially--

12:14.400 --> 12:15.317
Hey!

12:19.530 --> 12:22.658
You've got to be kidding me,
you bastard...

12:25.536 --> 12:26.370
What?

12:26.829 --> 12:28.414
What are you so angry about, Eren?

12:28.873 --> 12:31.500
Did I say something wrong?

12:31.625 --> 12:33.919
If you want to die, just keep talking!

12:34.753 --> 12:35.880
Hold up, Eren.

12:36.714 --> 12:39.049
This isn't normal,
no matter how you look at it.

12:39.633 --> 12:41.385
Isn't that right, Bertholdt?

12:43.387 --> 12:44.722
If you know something,

12:45.055 --> 12:47.433
quit with the silence and say it.

12:48.225 --> 12:49.101
What?

12:51.812 --> 12:52.855
Reiner...

12:53.606 --> 12:54.565
You...

12:55.357 --> 12:56.942
are not a soldier, you know.

12:58.819 --> 12:59.820
You and I...

13:00.696 --> 13:02.114
are warriors.

13:13.083 --> 13:13.918
Reiner!

13:14.376 --> 13:15.294
What are you doing?

13:21.133 --> 13:22.009
Hey...

13:22.801 --> 13:23.636
Why...

13:26.639 --> 13:27.723
is Marco...

13:29.183 --> 13:30.309
getting eaten?

13:39.193 --> 13:40.027
Right.

13:40.778 --> 13:43.072
That's how it is.

13:49.495 --> 13:50.663
What?

13:52.831 --> 13:54.041
What's he doing?

13:55.918 --> 13:59.338
More or less, I think I've figured it out.

14:00.297 --> 14:01.799
I thought it was strange.

14:02.341 --> 14:06.178
Why would the guy who broke the wall
risk his life to save Conny?

14:07.179 --> 14:11.100
Everything he does is contradictory,
but he doesn't realize it himself.

14:11.600 --> 14:15.646
I don't know why he ended up like this,
but probably...

14:16.230 --> 14:19.817
he was originally a warrior
whose goal was to break the wall.

14:20.150 --> 14:22.653
But after pretending to be a soldier
for so long,

14:22.862 --> 14:25.656
he lost sight of who he was
and couldn't tell which one was real.

14:27.199 --> 14:28.033
No...

14:28.534 --> 14:30.995
Unable to bear the weight of his sins,

14:31.370 --> 14:33.455
and maintain emotional balance
within his heart,

14:33.706 --> 14:37.459
he convinced himself
he was a soldier protecting the wall.

14:37.960 --> 14:40.087
And in the end, he believed it.

14:41.297 --> 14:45.134
As a result, his heart was split
and his memories became broken.

14:45.718 --> 14:49.179
This must not be the first time
Reiner has talked and made no sense...

14:49.805 --> 14:52.224
judging by Bertholdt's grim expression.

14:53.934 --> 14:55.269
It's amazing, really.

14:55.728 --> 14:58.022
For someone excessively honest
like you to--

14:58.147 --> 14:59.023
Enough!

15:00.774 --> 15:02.401
Shut your mouth.

15:06.238 --> 15:07.239
Sorry.

15:07.865 --> 15:09.158
I pried too much.

15:13.829 --> 15:15.664
You've got to be kidding me.

15:17.374 --> 15:19.919
Why are you pretending
to be the victim here?

15:20.502 --> 15:21.962
What's your deal?

15:23.589 --> 15:27.927
What the hell were you thinking
when you talked to us on that day?

15:29.970 --> 15:31.639
Tell me, Bertholdt.

15:32.306 --> 15:34.475
I'm talking to you, you damn lackey.

15:35.559 --> 15:37.186
I told you everything

15:37.394 --> 15:39.188
while you looked at me right in the eyes.

15:39.730 --> 15:42.441
About the day my mother was eaten alive...

15:42.733 --> 15:45.945
Stop!

15:46.403 --> 15:47.571
Isn't that right?

15:48.197 --> 15:52.159
Thanks to the piece of the wall you kicked
that went flying straight to my house,

15:52.326 --> 15:54.703
my mother couldn't escape or run away.

15:55.955 --> 15:59.124
You remember, right? I told you my story.

16:00.793 --> 16:02.169
What were you thinking?

16:03.420 --> 16:06.006
What were you thinking when I told you?

16:10.803 --> 16:12.096
Back then...

16:14.306 --> 16:17.309
I thought I felt sorry for you.

16:22.690 --> 16:23.941
Right...

16:25.359 --> 16:26.735
I see...

16:28.153 --> 16:29.488
You guys...

16:30.406 --> 16:31.448
You guys...

16:31.949 --> 16:34.743
are neither soldiers nor warriors.

16:35.536 --> 16:37.246
You're just murderers.

16:38.205 --> 16:43.043
You're psychotic mass-murderers
who've killed countless innocent people!

16:43.252 --> 16:44.920
Don't you think I know that?

16:45.129 --> 16:47.423
I don't need you to tell me!

16:47.506 --> 16:51.051
Then don't pretend to have emotions
like you're one of us!

16:51.218 --> 16:53.345
You guys aren't even human anymore!

16:53.679 --> 16:56.640
It's you two who've turned this world
into a living hell!

16:56.807 --> 16:58.434
Does that make you happy, murderers?

16:58.517 --> 17:01.979
What are you after
by calling us murderers?

17:02.312 --> 17:03.772
Do you want us to regret it?

17:03.856 --> 17:05.190
Do you want us to apologize?

17:05.399 --> 17:06.817
Would that satisfy you?

17:07.234 --> 17:09.486
The people you thought we were
no longer exist!

17:09.987 --> 17:11.822
If screaming makes you feel better,

17:12.156 --> 17:14.158
then scream your damn head off!

17:27.963 --> 17:29.214
That's right...

17:31.091 --> 17:32.468
I'm still...

17:33.469 --> 17:34.636
too naive.

17:36.722 --> 17:37.806
I've...

17:38.599 --> 17:39.975
got to do what I can.

17:41.018 --> 17:42.144
Do what I can...

17:43.562 --> 17:44.605
to make you guys suffer

17:45.105 --> 17:47.357
and die in the worst way possible.

17:48.525 --> 17:49.568
You've got it coming.

17:58.368 --> 17:59.953
You can't be serious.

18:01.080 --> 18:01.997
What?

18:02.539 --> 18:03.707
Quit it, Eren.

18:04.333 --> 18:06.460
If you keep saying childish crap
like that,

18:06.710 --> 18:08.003
I've got no hope for you.

18:08.587 --> 18:09.546
What?

18:13.467 --> 18:15.010
Hey, Reiner.

18:17.554 --> 18:19.181
What's that monkey?

18:23.018 --> 18:25.229
Monkey? What do you mean?

18:25.521 --> 18:27.815
What? You don't know?

18:28.732 --> 18:29.983
That's surprising,

18:30.359 --> 18:32.820
given how much you two stared at it

18:32.903 --> 18:34.988
with stars in your eyes
like two little brats.

18:35.864 --> 18:36.824
That monkey...

18:38.075 --> 18:40.369
What's that? A monkey?

18:41.286 --> 18:42.329
Just listen.

18:43.247 --> 18:45.499
That monkey Beast Titan

18:45.874 --> 18:47.835
is what caused this recent disaster.

18:48.669 --> 18:50.921
That made the Titans rise
from within the wall.

18:52.256 --> 18:55.092
I wonder if he was trying
to assess our strength.

18:56.552 --> 18:59.221
That's where these guys are trying to get.

18:59.972 --> 19:01.431
If you guys get to him,

19:01.932 --> 19:04.309
you'll be able to go back home, right?

19:05.727 --> 19:07.771
Did you know this?

19:08.313 --> 19:10.899
What do you know? Tell me everything!

19:11.024 --> 19:14.153
Just wait.
I've got circumstances of my own.

19:14.236 --> 19:15.821
What do you mean by that?

19:17.281 --> 19:21.034
If you think killing these two
will bring an end to everything...

19:21.410 --> 19:23.996
-you're gravely mistaken.
-What?

19:24.371 --> 19:27.249
-Then who's the enemy?
-Enemy?

19:27.916 --> 19:30.002
-If I said that, the--
-Ymir!

19:30.627 --> 19:33.463
Do you think there's any future
for this world?

19:34.840 --> 19:38.051
If you know so much,
think about what you want to do.

19:38.635 --> 19:41.889
It's not out of the question
for you to join our side.

19:42.723 --> 19:44.099
And trust you?

19:44.725 --> 19:47.978
As if. You two don't even trust me.

19:48.395 --> 19:50.314
Wrong. We can trust you.

19:51.148 --> 19:52.566
Because your one goal...

19:54.026 --> 19:55.694
is to protect Christa.

19:58.488 --> 20:01.950
When it comes to her,
we should be able to trust one another.

20:02.576 --> 20:04.912
You might think that I'm joking...

20:05.495 --> 20:08.373
but is it that hard for you to believe

20:08.582 --> 20:10.792
that we might want the best
for Christa as well?

20:11.501 --> 20:12.336
Or would you rather

20:13.003 --> 20:16.381
put your hopes in Eren and rely on him?

20:16.798 --> 20:17.674
What?

20:21.345 --> 20:23.388
You're probably thinking your best chance

20:23.722 --> 20:26.308
is to use Eren to escape from here.

20:27.184 --> 20:28.852
Because if you're taken by us,

20:29.061 --> 20:31.146
there's little chance of your rescue.

20:32.439 --> 20:34.733
To be honest, that's pretty much true.

20:35.359 --> 20:36.568
Even if you come with us,

20:37.069 --> 20:39.321
we can't guarantee your safety.

20:40.197 --> 20:44.076
But if it's Christa we're talking about,
we might be able to do something for her.

20:47.537 --> 20:49.331
Will it be your petty life?

20:49.831 --> 20:51.375
Or Christa's future?

20:52.751 --> 20:54.253
It's up to you to decide.

20:55.921 --> 20:58.131
There's no future for this world?

20:58.548 --> 21:01.051
Why is that? What's this about a monkey?

21:01.385 --> 21:02.636
What's going on?

21:04.096 --> 21:04.972
Hey!

21:06.014 --> 21:08.600
Hey, say something! Who's the enemy?

21:10.602 --> 21:11.561
Ymir!

21:19.444 --> 21:20.487
Who knows...

21:21.613 --> 21:22.614
It's settled, then.

21:24.074 --> 21:25.450
Too bad, Eren.

21:36.336 --> 21:38.714
The Scouts are already...

21:41.508 --> 21:42.467
Damn it!

21:43.719 --> 21:44.720
Shit!

21:45.137 --> 21:47.014
Damn you, Ymir.

21:50.392 --> 21:53.020
There's just one hour left until sunset.

23:32.744 --> 23:34.704
As sunset swiftly approaches...

23:35.413 --> 23:36.915
the Scout Regiment closes in,

23:37.124 --> 23:40.210
intent on rescuing Eren
from Reiner and Bertholdt.

23:41.586 --> 23:44.214
The pair plot to make their escape,

23:44.422 --> 23:46.007
fleeing by the use of ODM gear.

23:47.425 --> 23:51.805
However, reflecting on her past
and emotions,

23:52.639 --> 23:54.683
Ymir offers a plan of her own.

23:56.309 --> 24:00.105
Next episode, "Children."
